<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Rapier privacy and terms</title><main><h1>Rapier privacy and terms</h1>
				<p>Rapier needs no account signup and uses no analytics or advertising. Your files stay on your device
					until you save, share, back up or sync them. Sync writes plain files to the storage you
					choose. You keep or delete local files; Delete forever removes notes and their history.</p>
				<p>When you send feedback, your report is recorded to help improve Rapier. Please avoid sensitive information.</p>
				<p>The Android editor has no Internet permission. It records audio only when you press Record, into your
					notes. Google Play handles purchases, reviews and optional plugin downloads under its policy.</p>
				<p>Sharing a document through the hosted agent door (mcp.rapier.website) sends the content you choose there
					for shared reading and editing. Its private workspace keeps the document, retained edit history, inspected
					passages, presence, selections and tool records. Authorized connections and secret document references
					control workspace access. Active use renews workspace expiry to 30 days; unchanged sync does not. Expired
					workspaces are cleared on their next request or deletion alarm. In the editor, you can delete the workspace
					or disconnect agents from that document. The door keeps creation and registration budget records for one
					hour and tool invocation budget records for one minute. Your assistant's host handles the conversation under
					its policy.</p>
				<p>Essential cookies remember the browser that approved connected apps for up to 90 days, guard consent,
					and authorize paired editors for up to 24 hours. OAuth access tokens expire after 15 minutes. Refresh grants
					and client registrations expire after 90 days without renewal. You can revoke a connected app at
					<a href="https://mcp.rapier.website/oauth/disconnect" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connected apps</a>.
					Revoking a connection preserves your hosted documents; delete their workspaces to remove them.</p>
				<p>Hosted exports keep an unchanged file copy. A download link lasts up to 24 hours within the workspace's
					lifetime, and is revoked when you delete the workspace or disconnect agents. Expired copies are cleared on
					the next workspace update or deletion.</p>
				<p>Cloudflare serves the page and door and sees what web requests show.</p>
				<h3 class="licenses-given">terms</h3>
				<p>Rapier is free software: AGPL-3.0-only for the editor; MIT for the Markdown standard and embed helper.
					Provided as is, without warranty where law allows. Keep your own copies. The door may change or close.</p>
				<p><strong>Jack Skipworth · hello@rapier.website · effective 15 October 2026</strong></p>
			</main></html>